{"lastcomment":"Fixed (agenda v19, commit 1868e61) — verified, not just designed.

Root cause, precise: `TOOL`/`RESTOCK`'s `weaponMissing`/`kitPickShort`/`activeFloors` all derived "what kit tier matters" from `projectKit(s)` alone, which is `null` whenever `A.project` is unset. With no project (base worked out, #67), IDLE's own role-work (`mineLane`/`safeDescend`, tier `underground`/`deep`) gets refused by `S.start`'s kit preflight every ~30s cycle — but `TOOL`/`RESTOCK` never look at THAT kit spec, so the shortfall it names is aimed at by nothing.

Choice argued before building, per the ask: neither a new idle rung nor a relaxed floor. A new rung would duplicate machinery `TOOL`/`RESTOCK` already have; relaxing the floor doesn't fix anything — a real project would still hit the exact same `kit_missing` ","ncomments":1,"state":"OPEN","title":"Idle kit-completion: bots sit IDLE 'not setting off half-kitted' while holding ample crafting materials"}

